# Gaze preprocessing — Study 2

`study2_eye_asc.py` converts raw EyeLink `.asc` recordings into CSVs which contain trial-level gaze measures.

## How to run

Run the study script three times but change the `mode` setting before each run:

| Mode | Gaze window | Output |
|------|-------------|--------|
| 1 | Response-period gaze for LE (learning phase), ES (experiential-symbolic) and EE (experiential-experiential); used for the main analyses | `Participant_ID_eye_response_phase.csv` |
| 2 | Feedback-period gaze during learning phase | `Participant_ID_eye_feedback_phase.csv` |
| 3 | All valid left/right fixations across the entire trial for each LE, ES and EE trial | `Participant_ID_eye_allfix_phase.csv` |

I don't really use mode 3; this was just to double check things.

Each output contains one row per main-task trial, including dwell times, fixation counts, first/final fixation measures, gaze switches and fixation sequences. Training trials are excluded. Each run also updates the study’s parser audit.

For response gaze, fixations starting at or before the recorded button response are retained in full, including any portion after the response. There is no explicit fixed button-press buffer. All-fixation mode still applies left/right region filtering.